{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Unstable,</b> because you were unstable like water." "<b>You shall not have preeminence.</b> You shall have no superiority. It ought to have been אַל תּוֹתַר with vav in the holem. Others said: only you were unstable like poured-out water, and you were not preeminent at all. But in my opinion, the word אַל is found only in the place of a command, although וְדֶרֶךְ נְתִיבָה אַל־מָוֶת (Proverbs 12:28) is found and is not a command. The meaning is: do not seek superiority, even though you were unstable like water, and the pattern of תוּתַר is like זָכוֹר מִלְחָמָה אַל־תּוֹסֶף (Job [40:32]). The Gaon [Saadia] said: even a thing as slight as water — you shall have no superiority. And פָּחַז is from the derivation אַנְשֵׁי רִקִים וּפֹחֲזִים (Judges 9:4), and פֹחֲזִים is not the reverse." "<b>Then you defiled.</b> From the day you defiled, my bed was removed — as though he said, עֲלֵה מֵעָלָי. You will also find the word עלה used in the sense of cutting off, as in אֱלִי אַל־תַּעַלֵנִי בְּחֶצִי יָמָי (Psalms 102:25). This passage is explicitly stated in Chronicles (1 Chronicles 5:1): וּבְחַלְלוֹ יְצוּעֵי אָבִיו. And he said concerning Judah that he is the leader, and the birthright belongs to Joseph. Others say: and let him not be reckoned for the birthright, so that the counting begins with Reuben."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites Job 40:32 by the older verse numbering (MT 40:32 = some editions 40:24); the citation text אל תוסף matches MT Job 40:32."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:27.791951164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}